Worst-case stall: 723.0 ms unlimited vs 89.6 ms at budget 128 (8.1x better)
Phase C bullet 1 (chunked prefill): worst-case stall cut 8.1x, from 19.2x the victim's median to 2.18x at budget 128. Target NOT met, and the residual is understood. Without fusion the ratio asymptotes near 2.5x because a step carrying a chunk runs TWO forward passes, one for the chunk and one for the decode batch. Fusion (bullet 2) removes that second pass, and here it helped at 1/3 budgets and hurt at 2/3: budget 128 2.18x->2.62x, budget 32 2.33x->2.31x, budget 8 2.34x->2.41x. Removing a forward pass is not automatically a win: the fused pass still carries the chunk's tokens alongside the decode's one, and at larger model geometry that single wider pass can cost more than the two narrower ones it replaced.

Wrote benchmarks\results\chunked_prefill.json
